   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Two shaders, one mix\n\nTwo **kubakub shader** nodes draw A (*plasma*) and B (*rings*). **kubakub shader mix** takes their `images` on `a` and\n`b`: `mix` 0 is A, 1 is B. `how` = *a cuts b* lets B come in where A is bright, a wipe in the shape of A's pattern;\n*a bends b* lets A push B around; *blend* is a plain fade. `curve` = *triangle* runs the mix there and back.\n\nEverything about a shader (preset, sliders, size, length) is set on its own node. To make B an **effect on A**\n(plasma seen through eight bit), no mix is needed: connect A's `images` to `image0` of shader B.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
